{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>An oven and stoves.</b> They are movable utensils, made of earthenware, and they have a hollow space inside, and one places the pot over the opening of the hollow; and both have their mouths at the top." "<b>He shall break down.</b> For earthenware utensils have no purification by immersion." "<b>And they shall be impure to you.</b> Lest you say: I am commanded to break them down — Scripture says, ״וּטְמֵאִים יִהְיוּ לָכֶם״ — if he wishes to keep them in their impurity, he is permitted."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:55.739913671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}